The pseudo-application has
- a load method
- a save method
- a buffer
- a set of modes
  Each mode has
  - Some actions
  - Keybindings to those actions
  - a command loop
  - a view which renders the current state into the graphical primitives

(Some actions in a loop can switch modes.)

Separate from the pseudo-application are the graphical primitives
- a title bar
- a status bar
- a menu area
- a main area

- It is the role of the graphical primitives to figure out the minimum
amount of redraw for each update.


================================================================
Line endings

When parsing a text file, need to be able to split text into lines

See Unicode TR14.

Mandatory breaks

U+000C Form Feed (FF)
U+000B Line Tabulation (VT)
U+2028 Line Separator (LS)
U+2029 Paragraph Separator (PS)

CR by itself, not followed by LF
CR+LF
LF by itself
NL by itself

